# Group-subgroup graph (crystod-group --parent SG --irrep IR [IR2 ...] --graph);
# testsuite section 20
# The nodes are the parent, every stratum of the irrep (for several irreps:
# of the direct sum, including the strata in which only some irreps condense)
# and the kernel, layered by index; a line joins a group to each of its
# maximal subgroups among the nodes, up to conjugacy in the parent (some
# parent image of the fixed space of the larger group lies in the fixed space
# of the smaller one), transitively reduced. A line from the parent is dashed
# when the irrep that alone gives the stratum violates the Landau condition
# (cubic invariant) or the Lifshitz condition, so the transition cannot be
# continuous (M1+ of Pm-3m below); lines between strata are drawn solid
# (their continuity is not tested).
# Files: SUBGROUP_<SG>_<irreps>.html (inline SVG; hover a node for its
# direction, irreps, size, index, conventional basis and origin), --output
# FILE renames it, --graph-dot also writes the Graphviz .dot file.
# Pm-3m R4+ M3+: the 15 tilt systems of Howard and Stokes, Acta Cryst. B54,
# 782-789 (1998), with the group-subgroup lines among them (25 lines, which
# their Fig. 1 draws; derived here from their Glazer patterns), plus the ten
# strata with an in-phase and an out-of-phase tilt about one axis (R-3,
# P2_1/c, Pmmn and second embeddings of P4/mbm, Cmcm, C2/m, C2/c, P2_1/m,
# P-1). I4/mmm X2+ X3-: the hybrid improper ferroelectric Cmc2_1 of the n = 2
# Ruddlesden-Popper perovskites below Cmcm and Cmce.

$ crystod-group --parent Pm-3m --irrep R4+ M3+ --graph --graph-dot

* Supergroup *
Pm-3m (No. 221)

* Coupled irreps *
R4+: order parameter dimension 3
  Landau condition: satisfied (no cubic invariant)
  Lifshitz condition: satisfied (no Lifshitz invariant)
  -> a continuous transition is allowed
M3+: order parameter dimension 3
  Landau condition: satisfied (no cubic invariant)
  Lifshitz condition: satisfied (no Lifshitz invariant)
  -> a continuous transition is allowed

